{"addedOn":10,"avgRating":["fa fa-star-o","fa fa-star-o","fa fa-star-o","fa fa-star-o","fa fa-star-o"],"breadcrumbsHtml":"<a href=\"https://docs-be.progress.com/bundle/openedge-abl-reference-117\">OpenEdge Development: ABL Reference</a>\n<span><i class=\"fa fa-angle-right\"></i>\n</span>\n<a href=\"https://docs-be.progress.com/bundle/openedge-abl-reference-117/page/ABL-Syntax-Reference.html\">ABL Syntax Reference</a>\n<span><i class=\"fa fa-angle-right\"></i>\n</span>\n<span class=\"active\">/ Division operator</span>\n","class":"manual","created":2879,"dislikeurl":"https://docs-be.progress.com/dislike/309346","html":"<article class=\"hascomments\" data-page=\"bundle:openedge-abl-reference-117/enus/Division-operator.html\" id=\"bundle:openedge-abl-reference-117/enus/Division-operator.html\"><main role=\"main\"><article aria-labelledby=\"ariaid-title1\" class=\"dita\" id=\"Division-operator\" role=\"article\">\n  <h1 class=\"title topictitle1 reference\" id=\"ariaid-title1\">/ Division operator</h1>\n  \n  <div class=\"body refbody\">\n    <section class=\"section\">\n      <p class=\"p\">Divides one numeric expression by another numeric expression,\nproducing a decimal result. This is the case for both INTEGER and INT64\nexpressions.</p>\n    </section>\n    <section class=\"section\" id=\"Division-operator__syntax_GC152S2679231\"><h2 class=\"title sectiontitle\" id=\"d159402e101\">Syntax</h2>\n      \n      <table class=\"table frame-all\" id=\"Division-operator__idGDE1VQ2661824\"><caption></caption><colgroup><col style=\"width:100%\" /></colgroup><tbody class=\"tbody\">\n            <tr class=\"row rowsep-0\">\n              <td class=\"entry colsep-1 rowsep-1\">\n                <pre class=\"pre codeblock\"><code><var class=\"keyword varname\">expression</var> / <var class=\"keyword varname\">expression</var></code></pre>\n              </td>\n            </tr>\n          </tbody></table>\n      <dl class=\"dl parml\">\n        \n          <dt class=\"dt pt dlterm\">\n            <var class=\"keyword varname\">expression</var>\n          </dt>\n          <dd class=\"dd pd\">An expression that evaluates to a numeric value.</dd>\n        \n      </dl>\n    </section>\n    <section class=\"section\" id=\"Division-operator__example_GC152T2679237\"><h2 class=\"title sectiontitle\" id=\"d159402e146\">Example</h2>\n      \n      <p class=\"p\">This\nprocedure divides the number of items allocated by the number of items\non hand, producing a decimal value. The multiplication operator\n(*) converts that decimal value to a percentage.</p>\n      <p class=\"p\">\n        <strong class=\"ph b\">r-div.p</strong>\n      </p>\n      <table class=\"table frame-all\" id=\"Division-operator__idGDE1VR2661829\"><caption></caption><colgroup><col style=\"width:100%\" /></colgroup><tbody class=\"tbody\">\n            <tr class=\"row rowsep-0\">\n              <td class=\"entry colsep-1 rowsep-1\">\n                <pre class=\"pre codeblock\"><code>DISPLAY &quot;INVENTORY COMMITMENTS AS A PERCENT OF UNITS ON HAND&quot;.\nFOR EACH Item NO-LOCK:\n  DISPLAY Item.ItemNum Item.ItemName Item.Allocated Item.OnHand \n   (<strong class=\"ph b\">Item.Allocated / Item.OnHand</strong>) * 100 FORMAT &quot;&gt;&gt;9&quot; LABEL &quot;PCT&quot;.\nEND.</code></pre>\n              </td>\n            </tr>\n          </tbody></table>\n    </section>\n    <section class=\"section\" id=\"Division-operator__notes_GC152U2679243\"><h2 class=\"title sectiontitle\" id=\"d159402e184\">Notes</h2>\n      \n      <ul class=\"ul\">\n        <li class=\"li\">ABL <strong class=\"ph b\">always</strong> performs\ndivision as a decimal operation (the product of 5 / 2 is 2.5, not\n2). If you assign the result to an integer field, ABL rounds the\ndecimal to make the assignment. When you want ABL to truncate a\nquotient to an integer, use the TRUNCATE function (TRUNCATE(5 /\n2, 0) is 2). </li>\n        <li class=\"li\">The result of dividing a number by 0 is the Unknown value (<code class=\"ph codeph\">?</code>),\nand the AVM does not display an error message.</li>\n      </ul>\n    </section>\n    <section class=\"section\" id=\"Division-operator__see-also_GC152V2679251\"><h2 class=\"title sectiontitle\" id=\"d159402e205\">See also</h2>\n      \n      <p class=\"p\">\n        <a class=\"xref\" data-bundleid=\"openedge-abl-reference-117\" data-navpath=\"Multiplication-operator.html\" href=\"https://docs-be.progress.com/bundle/openedge-abl-reference-117/page/Multiplication-operator.html\">* Multiplication operator</a>\n      </p>\n    </section>\n  </div>\n<nav role=\"navigation\"><div class=\"familylinks\"><div class=\"previouslink\"><strong>Previous topic:</strong> <a class=\"link\" data-bundleid=\"openedge-abl-reference-117\" data-navpath=\"Multiplication-operator.html\" href=\"https://docs-be.progress.com/bundle/openedge-abl-reference-117/page/Multiplication-operator.html\">* Multiplication operator</a></div><div class=\"nextlink\"><strong>Next topic:</strong> <a class=\"link\" data-bundleid=\"openedge-abl-reference-117\" data-navpath=\"ABSOLUTE-function.html\" href=\"https://docs-be.progress.com/bundle/openedge-abl-reference-117/page/ABSOLUTE-function.html\">ABSOLUTE function</a></div></div></nav><nav class=\"related-links\" role=\"navigation\"></nav></article></main></article>\n","isWatched":false,"labelText":"Product; Product > OpenEdge; Product > OpenEdge > Version 11.7; Format; Format > Documentation","likes":0,"likeurl":"https://docs-be.progress.com/like/309346","myDocsURL":null,"numOfPageViews":0,"numOfRatingsText":"<span>0 Ratings","revised":2879,"showWatch":false,"topicMeta":[["bookowner","oe11docs"],["bookrights","oe11docs"],["bundle","openedge-abl-reference-117"],["data","OEInformationHub/Product"],["data","OEInformationHub/Product/product_openedge"],["data","OEInformationHub/Product/product_openedge/product_openedge_117"],["data","OEInformationHub/format"],["data","OEInformationHub/format/format_documentation"],["organization","oe11docs"]],"topicTitle":"/ Division operator","topicurl":"https://docs-be.progress.com/bundle/openedge-abl-reference-117/page/Division-operator.html","type":"Manual"}